  ],
  "text": "One of these planets spins backwards. Eight planets. Here is what makes each one strange. Mercury has no atmosphere, so its sky is always black. Venus spins backwards, and a day there lasts longer than its year. Earth is the only place we have ever found life. Mars is red because its soil is basically rust. Jupiter's great red spot is a storm wider than Earth. Saturn is so light it would float in water. Uranus is tipped on its side, rolling around the sun. And on Neptune, the wind blows faster than the speed of sound. Follow for one fact a day.",
